      "text": "Historic Mexico City, market visits and flight to Cancún"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "713124679f788ad134afd89ce8ad813fac5d5a1868167cef590ac1e974122acf",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-63081f33d4c840e99362579a12d8b39a",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel.\n\nToday you’ll explore the historic centre of Mexico City, built by the Spanish on the ruins of Tenochtitlan, the ancient Aztec capital. At its centre is the vast El Zócalo square, where you’ll visit the Metropolitan Cathedral, the largest church in Latin America.\n\nYou’ll then visit the Plaza de las Tres Culturas, where traces of the Aztec civilisation, the Spanish colonial era and modern Mexico stand side by side.\n\nNext, explore San Juan Market in the city centre and Medellín Market in the Roma district. Stalls are stocked with exotic fruit, fresh vegetables, herbs and spices. You’ll find mole, maize, fish, meat, many varieties of chilli, flowers and plants, natural remedies, household goods and kitchenware. As you browse, you can try a fresh fruit juice and a hot quesadilla.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to Mexico City International Airport for your flight to Cancún. The flight is excluded.\n\nOn arrival, you’ll be met and taken by private transfer to the five-star Presidente Intercontinental Cancún."
    },
